Golden boot log -- zynqmp_apu, default configuration (no fault injection)
========================================================================

The reference every "boot log identical" acceptance criterion in
PLAN_driver_model.md §2.1 is diffed against. Captured from the ZCU102 A53
console, hardware-verified.

Provenance
----------
Zephyr build : v4.4.0-7880-g90a9cb34e850
Commit       : 90a9cb34e85 ("samples: ad9081: add the driver-model conversion
               plan")
Tree state   : that commit PLUS the uncommitted conversion of plan steps 1 and
               6 -- src/spi_mmio_fixup.c consolidating the SPI mapping hooks
               (§1.5), and hmc7044 as an adi,hmc7044 clock_control driver
               (§1.3). The version string above therefore names HEAD, not the
               exact tree; do not read it as "this is plain 90a9cb34e85".

               Captured while that driver still lived in the sample's src/. It
               has since moved to drivers/clock_control/clock_control_hmc7044.c
               with no functional change -- same registers, same log lines, and
               a byte-identical zephyr.bin size -- so this log remains the
               correct reference. The move is not reflected in the output
               because it does not alter any.
Board        : ZCU102, AD9082 (prod_id 0x9082, grade 0x2, rev 0x3)
Bitstream    : zcu102_ad9081_m8_l4 -- M8/L4/F4/K32/S1/NP16, TX link-mode 9,
               RX link-mode 10, 8B10B subclass 1
Config       : prj.conf only (CONFIG_AD9081_FAULT_INJECTION=n)

How to capture a comparable log
-------------------------------
    west build -p always -b zynqmp_apu samples/boards/amd/ad9081_chipid
    # flash the PL bitstream, then from u-boot:
    #   go <load addr>    (with zephyr.bin -- not bootelf)
    # console on the ZCU102 USB-UART

Reading a diff against this file
--------------------------------
Timestamps and addresses vary run to run and are not part of the comparison.
What matters is that every line is present, in this order, with the same
content. Three specific things a future step is likely to perturb, called out
so they are not mistaken for noise:

  * The two "SUCCESS: HMC7044 ..." lines appear BEFORE the
    "*** Booting Zephyr OS ***" banner. That is correct as of step 6: the
    HMC7044 is a clock_control driver and programmes itself at POST_KERNEL,
    before main() runs. Any block converted to the driver model will migrate
    its own log lines above the banner the same way.

  * "GT refclk from hmc7044@0 out12: 500000 kHz" is a queried rate, not a
    constant. If the HMC7044 devicetree changes, this and the two
    "GT dividers programmed for ... @ N kHz ref" lines change with it, and
    axi_adxcvr additionally logs a warning that the bitstream was synthesised
    for 500000 kHz.

  * The first console line ("Starting application at ...") is u-boot's, with a
    truncated final character -- the UART is still switching over. It is not
    Zephyr output and carries no information.

  * The TPL clk_freq values alternate between 0x00027fff and 0x00028000 across
    otherwise identical runs -- a measured ratio, off by one LSB depending on
    where the counter is sampled. Either value on either TPL line is fine.

Known-good values worth checking explicitly
-------------------------------------------
  PLL1 N1=10 R1=1 PFD1=10000 kHz          PLL1 locked on CLKIN0 @ 100 MHz
  PLL2 N2=15 R2=1 doubler=1 VCO=high      PLL2 locked @ 3000.000000 MHz
  GT refclk 500000 kHz, lane rate 10000000 kHz
  jesd204-tx status 0x00000013 [DATA]     jesd204-rx status 0x00000003 [DATA]
  all 4 RX lanes in sync
  chip JTX (framer) 0x007d                chip JRX (deframer) 0x000f

This file covers the default build only. The fault-injection configuration has
its own reference: boot_log_fi.golden, whose bring-up prefix matches this one
line for line before the FI checks begin.

